dictive modeling.\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column B01[C-Br] is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['B01[C-Br]'], inplace=True)\n# B01[C-Br] is a binary column with almost all 0 values (Mean = 0.0411, highly skewed), reducing its informativeness for the downstream task. Features with predominantly one-sided distribution often lack predictive power.\n```end\n\n```python\n# Explanation why the column nCRX3 is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=['nCRX3'], inplace=True)\n# nCRX3 has very low variance (Q3 = 0.0, Mean = 0.0253, Std = 0.2012), suggesting it adds minimal meaningful variation to the data and is unlikely to contribute significantly to prediction performance.\n```end", 'Here are three possible feature engineering steps to improve predictions for classifying chemicals into "ready" or "not ready" biodegradable:\n\n### Step 1: Interaction Features\nCertain chemical attributes might interact to influence biodegradability, so creating interaction terms (e.g., multiplying or dividing features) could capture these interactions.\n\n```python\n# nO_SpMax_L_ratio\n# Ratio between the number of oxygen atoms (nO) and the leading eigenvalue from Laplace matrix (SpMax_L).\n# Usefulness: High oxygen content may interact with molecular topology (SpMax_L) to better capture the chemical\'s environmental reactivity and consequent biodegradability.\ndf[\'nO_SpMax_L_ratio\'] = df[\'nO\'] / (df[\'SpMax_L\'] + 1e-10)\n\n# C%_nCb-_interaction\n# Interaction between percentage of carbon atoms (C%) and number of substituted benzene C(sp2) (nCb-).\n# Usefulness: This helps model how the aromatic content (nCb-) correlates with the carbon composition, which may influence chemical complexity and readiness for biodegradation.\ndf[\'C%_nCb-_interaction\'] = df[\'C%\'] * df[\'nCb-\']\n\n# SpMax_L_Ti2L_diff\n# Difference between the leading eigenvalue from Laplace matrix (SpMax_L) and the second Mohar index (Ti2_L).\n# Usefulness: These molecular descriptors relate to the topology of the molecule, and their difference might represent specific structural variations linked to biodegradability.\ndf[\'SpMax_L_Ti2L_diff\'] = df[\'SpMax_L\'] - df[\'TI2_L\']\n```end  \n\n### Step 2: Non-linear Transformations\nApplying non-linear transformations (e.g., square, log, and exponential) can help model non-linear relationships in the data.\n\n```python\n# log_nN\n# Log transformation of the number of Nitrogen atoms (nN).\n# Usefulness: Nitrogen presence may influence biodegradability non-linearly; a log scale handles large variance effectively.\ndf[\'log_nN\'] = np.log1p(df[\'nN\'])\n\n# sqrt_F03C-O\n# Square root transformation of the frequency of C-O bonds at topological distance 3 (F03[C-O]).\n# Usefulness: Reduces the impact of outliers in this feature while preserving its relative order and potential importance in interactions with condensation reactions.\ndf[\'sqrt_F03C-O\'] = np.sqrt(df[\'F03[C-O]\'])\n\n# SpMax_B_cube\n# Cube transformation of the leading eigenvalue from Burden matrix weighted by mass (SpMax_B(m)).\n# Usefulness: Highlights extreme values of the structural feature for specific edge cases that may drive biodegradability.\ndf[\'SpMax_B_cube\'] = df[\'SpMax_B(m)\'] ** 3\n```end  \n\n### Step 3: Statistical Encoding and Dimensionality Reduction\nReduce noise or sparsity in features by encoding or mixing features into aggregate statistical representations.\n\n```python\n# nC_H_ratio\n# Ratio of number of heavy atoms (nHM) to the number of Hydrogen donor atoms (nHDon).\n# Usefulness: Captures the balance of molecular density versus hydrogen donors affecting biodegradation likelihood.\ndf[\'nC_H_ratio\'] = df[\'nHM\'] / (df[\'nHDon\'] + 1e-10)\n\n# zscore_SdO\n# Z-score normalization of the sum of dO E-states (SdO).\n# Usefulness: Centers and scales the feature, which has a wide range and could dominate other features unfairly in the model.\ndf[\'zscore_SdO\'] = (df[\'SdO\'] - df[\'SdO\'].mean()) / (df[\'SdO\'].std() + 1e-10)\n\n# SdssC_F04C-N_rolling_mean\n# Rolling mean of the sum of dssC E-states (SdssC) and frequency of C-N bonds at topological distance 4 (F04[C-N]).\n# Usefulness: Captures short-term trends or temporal pairing effects in closely related molecular components that might indicate biodegradability.\ndf[\'SdssC_F04C-N_rolling_mean\'] = (df[\'SdssC\'] + df[\'F04[C-N]\']).rolling(window=3, min_periods=1).mean()\n```end  \n\n### Dropped Columns\nSome features may be irrelevant or redundant due to low variability or poor utilization in the model. For example:\n```python\n# Explanation why the column nCrt is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=[\'nCrt\'], inplace=True)\n# nCrt (number of ring tertiary C(sp3)) has consistently low values (mean = 0.139, median = 0.0) across the dataset, providing minimal variability for the model to learn from.\n\n# Explanation why the column B01[C-Br] is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=[\'B01[C-Br]\'], inplace=True)\n# This feature (presence of C-Br at a short distance) has a near-zero mean and low frequency in the dataset, making it unlikely to contribute significantly to the model.\n\n# Explanation why the column N-073 is dropped\ndf.drop(columns=[\'N-073\'], inplace=True)\n# N-073 (specific nitrogen types) has low variance (mean = 0.025, median = 0.0) and adds minimal value due to its sparsity and limited distribution.\n```end']
