# Step 1: Interaction Features - Product of nCb- and nO
# Feature: nCbO_interaction
# Feature description: Interaction between the number of substituted benzene C(sp2) atoms (nCb-) and the number of oxygen atoms (nO) to explore their combined role in affecting biodegradability. 
# Usefulness: Certain combinations of oxygen atoms and aromatic structures could be more predictive of biodegradability due to their functional relationships in chemical reactivity and molecular structure.

df['nCbO_interaction'] = df['nCb-'] * df['nO']
end

python
# Step 2: Non-linear transformation - Log of SdO (Sum of dO E-states)
# Feature: log_SdO
# Feature description: Applies logarithmic transformation to SdO to capture the diminishing effect of high values while highlighting subtle differences in smaller ranges.
# Usefulness: High values of SdO might have disproportionate influence on biodegradability, so capturing the non-linear behavior of this feature can help the model better learn important patterns.

df['log_SdO'] = df['SdO'].apply(lambda x: np.log(x + 1))  # Adding 1 to handle zero values safely.
end

python
# Step 3: Ratio Feature - nCp / C%
# Feature: nCp_to_C_ratio
# Feature description: Calculates the ratio of terminal primary C(sp3) atoms (nCp) to the percentage of C atoms (C%) to understand the relative density of reactive primary carbons in the molecule.
# Usefulness: Higher density of primary carbons might correlate with higher reactivity and thus impact biodegradability. This feature captures such relative density relationships.

df['nCp_to_C_ratio'] = df['nCp'] / (df['C%'] + 0.001)  # Adding 0.001 to avoid division by zero.
end

python
